# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. That file is gitignored.
# The same values go into GitHub repo Settings → Secrets and variables →
# Actions, so the deploy workflow can build with them.
#
# None of these are secrets in the "must never be seen" sense — Vite inlines
# them into the JS bundle and anyone can read them there. That is normal and
# expected for a static site. Your actual security is:
#   1. Firestore rules restricting reads/writes to your two UIDs
#   2. Firebase sign-up disabled, so the API key can't be used to self-register
#   3. An HTTP referrer restriction on the Maps key, so it only works on your domain

# Firebase → Project settings → General → Your apps → SDK setup and configuration
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# Google Cloud → APIs & Services → Credentials (restrict this by HTTP referrer!)
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
# Google Cloud → Google Maps Platform → Map management → create a Map ID.
# Required for the custom Y2K map styling and for advanced markers.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID=
